Both fit tests passed, so the 1,024-token and 2,048-token chunk arms both fit in GPU memory. I measured their speeds and queued the control's whole training chain plus the 1,024-token arm behind the running control. There are no accuracy numbers yet.

## Done this wake
- **2,048-token chunks:** fits on 4 A100-80GB at batch 3 per GPU, about 72 GB per GPU. 58.6 s per step, so a full stage 1 (text pretraining, 1M documents) takes about 85 h. Test closed.
- **1,024-token chunks:** fits at batch 6 per GPU, about 71 GB per GPU. 42.1 s per step, so a full stage 1 takes about 61 h. Test closed.
- **Training-setting differences:** I compared the resolved training settings of the control and the long-chunk runs. Only the chunk length, the text kept per document and the batch split differ. The effective batch stays at 192 documents.
- **Campaign rules:** I wrote the measured speeds into the rules. I also added two data settings the stage-2 and finetune commands need. They were left out of the written command lines, and without them the scripts would train on their default data. I copied them from the old reference runs' saved configs.

## Running now
- **Control stage 1 (256-token chunks):** running since 03:47 at 11.6 s per step. It should finish around 20:45 today, well inside its 23 h limit. Its first check of the loss on held-out text comes at step 2,000, around 10:15.
- **Queued behind it (5 jobs), each starting only when the job before it succeeds:**
  - the 1,024-token arm's stage 1 (76 h limit);
  - the control's stage 2 (images), then its two finetunes (seeds 42 and 43);
  - a check that each compressed slot still holds its own part of the text, on the control's stage-1 model.

## Budget warning (no action yet)
At the measured speeds, all three arms use about 35.0 of the 35 GPU-days allowed. That leaves nothing for reruns or a third seed. The control plus the 1,024-token arm come to about 18.4 GPU-days. I added a rule: the 2,048-token arm starts only if it still fits in the budget. If not, I will ask you around 2026-11-14, when the 1,024-token stage 1 ends.

## Next wake
At the step-2,000 checkpoint, or when the control's stage 1 ends, at most 8 h from now. I will check that the control has not collapsed (loss flat or NaN). If it has, I cancel it and every job chained behind it.

I reported two expmon problems:
